{"76":{"n":76,"cl":826,"id":"pg-2701-1419","type":"passage","cat":"text","title":"Moby Dick; Or, The Whale","creator":"Herman Melville","date":"1891","source":{"institution":"Project Gutenberg","work":"Moby Dick; Or, The Whale","url":"https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/2701"},"rights":{"license":"PDM"},"editorial":{"note":"","noteSource":"source","room":"words","tags":["19th-century","prose","adventure-stories","ahab","mentally-ill","psychological-fiction"],"tone":"sun","quality":1.182},"text":{"body":"The first boat we read of, floated on an ocean, that with Portuguese vengeance had whelmed a whole world without leaving so much as a widow. That same ocean rolls now; that same ocean destroyed the wrecked ships of last year. Yea, foolish mortals, Noah’s flood is not yet subsided; two thirds of the fair world it yet covers.","verse":false}},"110":{"n":110,"cl":826,"id":"pg-1727-234","type":"passage","cat":"text","title":"The Odyssey: Rendered into English prose for the use of those who cannot read the original","creator":"Homer","date":"-650","source":{"institution":"Project Gutenberg","work":"The Odyssey: Rendered into English prose for the use of those who cannot read the original","url":"https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/1727"},"rights":{"license":"PDM"},"editorial":{"note":"","noteSource":"source","room":"words","tags":["ancient","prose","epic-poetry","greek","homer","odysseus"],"tone":"ink","quality":1.077},"text":{"body":"Meantime the suitors went on board and sailed their ways over the sea, intent on murdering Telemachus. Now there is a rocky islet called Asteris, of no great size, in mid channel between Ithaca and Samos, and there is a harbour on either side of it where a ship can lie. Here then the Achaeans placed themselves in ambush.","verse":false}},"9339":{"n":9339,"cl":826,"id":"eu-91660_SMVK_EM_video_3256521","type":"video","cat":"video","title":"Världsomsegling 1880-tal, bildspel","creator":"Unknown","date":"","source":{"institution":"Museum of Ethnograph